<title>UK: BT up on positive comment after Swiss move.</title>
<headline>BT up on positive comment after Swiss move.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Telecommunications Plc rose on Monday amid positive comment on the stock following Friday's announcement that BT and TeleDanmark were buying a 49 percent stake in a new Swiss telecoms group.</p>
<p>BT shares were up 4-1/2p at 395 by 1203 GMT in active trading of 4.2 million shares.</p>
<p>Analysts at SBC Warburg repeated a &quot;buy&quot; recommendation on BT shares following the Swiss move, saying Switzerland is one of the most attractive markets for a second operator to enter and compete in.</p>
<p>The SBC Warburg analysts said Switzerland has nearly four times the normal volume of international calls as the average in Europe.</p>
<p>On Friday, Switzerland's Newtelco, a group including the Swiss Federal Railways and retailer Migros, said it picked BT and TeleDanmark as its international partners.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
